# BMS Modal Design Rules

These rules apply to every Ant Design `Modal` rendered in this app. Brand
color is **`#962E32`** (burgundy), darker hover variant **`#7A2326`**.

## 1. Header Bar

Every modal must use a solid burgundy header bar — **no native AntD header,
no gradients, no chips**.

- Bar height: `40px` (`h-10`)
- Background: solid `#962E32`, edge-to-edge (no rounded clipping on its own)
- Title: white, `text-sm`, `font-semibold`, left-aligned
- Close icon: white `X` on the right, with a subtle `hover:bg-white/15` halo
- Use `closable={false}` on the `Modal` and render a custom header `<div>`
  as the first child of the modal body
- Modal `styles` must set `body: { padding: 0 }` and
  `content: { padding: 0, overflow: 'hidden' }` so the bar reaches the edges

Example:

```jsx
<Modal
    open={open}
    onCancel={onClose}
    footer={null}
    centered
    destroyOnClose
    title={null}
    closable={false}
    styles={{ body: { padding: 0 }, content: { padding: 0, overflow: 'hidden' } }}
>
    <div className="flex h-10 items-center justify-between bg-[#962E32] px-4 text-white">
        <h2 className="m-0 text-sm font-semibold leading-none text-white">
            {/* Modal title */}
        </h2>
        <button
            type="button"
            aria-label="Close"
            onClick={onClose}
            className="flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded text-white transition hover:bg-white/15 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-white/40"
        >
            {/* X icon */}
        </button>
    </div>

    {/* ...content... */}
    {/* ...footer... */}
</Modal>
```

## 2. Footer Button Placement

Every modal footer must keep all buttons grouped on the **right side**.

- Action buttons (`Update`, `Save`, `Submit`, `Delete`, etc.) appear immediately
  to the left of `Close`.
- `Close` (or `Cancel`) is always the rightmost button.
- Primary action is solid burgundy (`#962E32` / `#7A2326` on hover) with a
  relevant `lucide-react` icon.

```jsx
<div className="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-6 py-3">
    {/* Primary / secondary actions: Update, Save, etc. */}
    <Button onClick={onClose}>Close</Button>
</div>
```

## 3. Section Headings, Labels & Values

Inside modals (and any read-only data display in the app):

- **Section headings** (group titles such as "Vehicle Information",
  "Account & Identifiers") use the brand burgundy color `#962E32`,
  **UPPERCASE**, `text-xs`, `font-semibold`, tracked
  (`tracking-[0.12em]`), with a thin slate divider underneath.
- **Field labels** use the brand burgundy color `#962E32`, **camel/title
  case** (e.g. `Plate Number`, `RFID Tag`), small text, `font-semibold`,
  and light tracking (`tracking-[0.01em]` or similar). Do not force field
  labels to uppercase.
- **Values** use solid **black** (`text-black` / `#000000`), `text-sm`
  unless the value is meant to be visually prominent (e.g. plate number).
- Empty / missing values render as `N/A` in a muted slate tone
  (`text-slate-400`) — never burgundy and never black.

```jsx
{/* Section heading */}
<h4
    className="mb-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-1.5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]"
    style={{ color: '#962E32' }}
>
    Vehicle Information
</h4>

{/* Field label + value */}
<div className="min-w-0 py-1.5">
    <span
        className="block text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.01em]"
        style={{ color: '#962E32' }}
    >
        {label}
    </span>
    <div className="mt-0.5 text-sm font-medium text-black">
        {value ?? <span className="text-slate-400">N/A</span>}
    </div>
</div>
```

## 4. Don't

- ❌ Do not use AntD's default modal title bar (white header with dark text)
- ❌ Do not spread action buttons to the far left
- ❌ Do not put `Close` on the left or between action buttons
- ❌ Do not use blue / indigo / sky colors anywhere in a modal
- ❌ Do not color values burgundy or color labels black — labels are burgundy,
  values are black
- ❌ Do not use `uppercase` on field labels (it is required on section headings only)
- ❌ Do not write section headings in title case (they must be uppercase)
